(3. Solution to Question 2: Incline Force Resolution) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Given: 10.0 kg crate on 30 degree frictionless slope. Gravitational acceleration g = 9.80 m/s^2.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Parallel component: F_parallel = m * g * sin\(30 deg\) = 10.0 * 9.80 * 0.50 = 49.0 N.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Perpendicular normal force: F_N = m * g * cos\(30 deg\) = 10.0 * 9.80 * 0.866 = 84.87 N.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
0 -14 Td
(Conclusion: Acceleration down the incline a = g * sin\(30 deg\) = 4.90 m/s^2 independent of mass.) Tj
